  "answer_text": "Great question \u2014 and honestly, there's no single \"correct\" answer, but here's a breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## How to Pronounce \"Doge\" \ud83d\udc15\n\n### The Most Widely Accepted Pronunciation (The Meme/Dogecoin)\nThe most commonly accepted pronunciation of Doge (as in the meme and Dogecoin) is **\"dohj\"** (rhymes with \"rogue\" but with a J sound), written as /do\u028a\u0292/ in IPA. This was confirmed by Dogecoin's co-creator Jackson Palmer, who said the name was inspired by the animated series *Homestar Runner*. In one of the episodes, a character spells out D-O-G-E and another character reads it as **\"dohj\"** (/do\u028a\u0292/).\n\n---\n\n### All the Common Pronunciations\n\nAccording to Wikipedia, the meme can be pronounced **/do\u028a\u0292/** (\"dohzh\"), **/do\u028ad\u0292/** (\"dohj\"), or **/do\u028a\u0261/** (\"dohg\"). Here's a breakdown of each:\n\n1. **\"Dohzh\"** (/do\u028a\u0292/) \u2014 Long O, soft G like in \"treasure.\" This is arguably the most media-recognized version.\n\n2. **\"Dohj\"** (/do\u028ad\u0292/) \u2014 Long O, soft G like in \"judge.\" This pronunciation is widely believed to have originated with a Tumblr user who submitted a computer-read audio file to a site called \"Your Daily Doge,\" though it's also been attributed to a 2005 puppet episode of *Homestar Runner*.\n\n3. **\"Dohg\"** (/do\u028a\u0261/) \u2014 Long O, hard G (rhymes with \"vogue\" or \"rogue\"). The logic here is that the original word \"dog\" has a hard G, so the E only modifies the vowel, not the consonant \u2014 sort of like how \"slop\" becomes \"slope.\"\n\n4. **\"Doh-geh\"** \u2014 Long O, hard G, spoken E (like \"doggy\" with an accent). Some prefer this because it sounds like a bastardized version of \"doggy.\"\n\n---\n\n### The Historical \"Doge\" (Venice)\nThere's also the historical pronunciation of \"Doge\" \u2014 the name for the chief magistrate of Venice \u2014 which is pronounced the same as \"dohj,\" so it's entirely possible this pronunciation feels older and more established to some people.\n\n---\n\n### TL;DR\n- \u2705 Most accepted (by meme/Dogecoin creators): **\"Dohj\"** or **\"Dohzh\"**\n- \ud83d\udd01 Also common: **\"Dohg\"** (rhymes with vogue)\n- Much debate. Very pronunciation. Wow.",
